RECORD = HEAD THEEDGERANGEI THEEDGENTOKENIZER TEMPLATELITERALARRAYGENERATOR REGEXPTEMPLATELITERALFUNCTION SELFCONTAINEDPROXYREFLECT THEFULLPIPELINE WRAPTHEREGEXINASELFCONTAINEDPROXY THEEDGENPARAMETERASTHEDOF SELFCONTAINEDNOEXTERNALDEPENDENCIES THEWHOLETHINGASONEOBJECT .

HEAD =
  "// i151.ts — I-151: edge-n-tokenizer → TemplateLiteralArray → RegExp → Proxy/Reflect"
  "import assert from ""node:assert"";"
  .

THEEDGERANGEI =
  "// ── 1. The edge range (I-113) ──────────────────────────────────"
  "// Vertex: 0x0-0x1 ; Edge: 0x2-0x7 ; Face: cells in 0x0-0x7 grid"
  "const VERTEX = [0x0, 0x1] as const;"
  "const EDGE   = [0x2, 0x3, 0x4, 0x5, 0x6, 0x7] as const;"
  "assert.strictEqual(VERTEX.length, 2, ""2 vertex values"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(EDGE.length, 6, ""6 edge values"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(VERTEX.length + EDGE.length, 8, ""V + E = octet"");"
  .

THEEDGENTOKENIZER =
  "// ── 2. The edge-n-tokenizer ────────────────────────────────────"
  "// Tokenize a byte buffer at the edge boundary values."
  "// n = the number of edge tokens to accumulate before emitting."
  "type Token = { kind: ""edge"" | ""data""; value: number; index: number };"
  "function edgeNTokenize(buf: Uint8Array, n: number): Token[] {"
  "  const tokens: Token[] = [];"
  "  const edgeSet = new Set(EDGE as readonly number[]);"
  "  let dataRun: number[] = [];"
  "  let runStart = 0;"
  "  for (let i = 0; i < buf.length; i++) {"
  "    if (edgeSet.has(buf[i])) {"
  "      if (dataRun.length > 0) {"
  "        for (let j = 0; j < dataRun.length; j++) {"
  "          tokens.push({ kind: ""data"", value: dataRun[j], index: runStart + j });"
  "        }"
  "        dataRun = [];"
  "      }"
  "      tokens.push({ kind: ""edge"", value: buf[i], index: i });"
  "    } else {"
  "      if (dataRun.length === 0) runStart = i;"
  "      dataRun.push(buf[i]);"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  if (dataRun.length > 0) {"
  "    for (let j = 0; j < dataRun.length; j++) {"
  "      tokens.push({ kind: ""data"", value: dataRun[j], index: runStart + j });"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  // group edge tokens into runs of n"
  "  const grouped: Token[] = [];"
  "  let edgeRun: Token[] = [];"
  "  for (const t of tokens) {"
  "    if (t.kind === ""edge"") {"
  "      edgeRun.push(t);"
  "      if (edgeRun.length === n) {"
  "        grouped.push(...edgeRun);"
  "        edgeRun = [];"
  "      }"
  "    } else {"
  "      if (edgeRun.length > 0) {"
  "        grouped.push(...edgeRun);"
  "        edgeRun = [];"
  "      }"
  "      grouped.push(t);"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  if (edgeRun.length > 0) grouped.push(...edgeRun);"
  "  return grouped;"
  "}"
  "// test"
  "const testBuf = new Uint8Array([0x41, 0x02, 0x42, 0x03, 0x43, 0x04, 0x44]);"
  "const tokens = edgeNTokenize(testBuf, 1);"
  "assert.ok(tokens.length > 0, ""tokenizer produces tokens"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(tokens.filter(t => t.kind === ""edge"").length, 3, ""3 edge tokens"");"
  .

TEMPLATELITERALARRAYGENERATOR =
  "// ── 3. TemplateLiteralArray generator ──────────────────────────"
  "// A tagged template that produces a TemplateLiteralArray."
  "function tagCapture(strings: TemplateStringsArray, ...values: unknown[]) {"
  "  return {"
  "    cooked: [...strings],"
  "    raw: [...(strings as any).raw ?? [...strings]],"
  "    values,"
  "    length: strings.length,"
  "  };"
  "}"
  "const captured = tagCapture`hello ${""world""} and ${1 + 2}`;"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(captured.cooked, [""hello "", "" and "", """"]);"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(captured.values, [""world"", 3]);"
  "assert.strictEqual(captured.length, 3);"
  .

REGEXPTEMPLATELITERALFUNCTION =
  "// ── 4. RegExp template literal function ────────────────────────"
  "// A tag function that builds a RegExp from a template."
  "function re(strings: TemplateStringsArray, ...values: unknown[]): RegExp {"
  "  let pattern = """";"
  "  for (let i = 0; i < strings.length; i++) {"
  "    pattern += strings[i];"
  "    if (i < values.length) {"
  "      const v = values[i];"
  "      pattern += typeof v === ""string"" ? v : String(v);"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  return new RegExp(pattern);"
  "}"
  "const rx = re`^a${""b""}+c$`;"
  "assert.ok(rx instanceof RegExp, ""re returns RegExp"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(rx.source, ""^ab+c$"", ""regex source built from template"");"
  "assert.ok(rx.test(""abbbc""), ""regex matches"");"
  "assert.ok(!rx.test(""ac""), ""regex rejects"");"
  .

SELFCONTAINEDPROXYREFLECT =
  "// ── 5. Self-contained Proxy/Reflect ─────────────────────────────"
  "// A Proxy whose handler forwards to Reflect. (I-135)"
  "function makeSelfContainedProxy<T extends object>(target: T) {"
  "  const handler: ProxyHandler<T> = {"
  "    get(t, p, r) { return Reflect.get(t, p, r); },"
  "    set(t, p, v, r) { return Reflect.set(t, p, v, r); },"
  "    has(t, p) { return Reflect.has(t, p); },"
  "    deleteProperty(t, p) { return Reflect.deleteProperty(t, p); },"
  "    ownKeys(t) { return Reflect.ownKeys(t); },"
  "    getOwnPropertyDescriptor(t, p) { return Reflect.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(t, p); },"
  "  };"
  "  return new Proxy(target, handler);"
  "}"
  "const obj = makeSelfContainedProxy({ a: 1, b: 2 });"
  "assert.strictEqual(obj.a, 1, ""proxy get a"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(obj.b, 2, ""proxy get b"");"
  "obj.c = 3;"
  "assert.strictEqual(obj.c, 3, ""proxy set c"");"
  "assert.ok(""c"" in obj, ""proxy has c"");"
  "delete (obj as any).c;"
  "assert.ok(!(""c"" in obj), ""proxy delete c"");"
  .

THEFULLPIPELINE =
  "// ── 6. The full pipeline ────────────────────────────────────────"
  "// Tokenizer -> template -> regex -> proxy"
  "function buildRegexFromBuffer(buf: Uint8Array, n: number): RegExp {"
  "  const tokens = edgeNTokenize(buf, n);"
  "  // build a template literal array from the token values"
  "  const parts: string[] = [];"
  "  const values: number[] = [];"
  "  for (const t of tokens) {"
  "    if (t.kind === ""edge"") {"
  "      parts.push("""");"
  "      values.push(t.value);"
  "    } else {"
  "      const ch = String.fromCharCode(t.value);"
  "      if (parts.length === 0) parts.push(ch);"
  "      else parts[parts.length - 1] += ch;"
  "    }"
  "  }"
  "  if (parts.length === 0) parts.push("""");"
  "  // simulate a tagged template"
  "  const strings = Object.assign(parts, { raw: [...parts] }) as unknown as TemplateStringsArray;"
  "  return re(strings, ...values.map(v => String.fromCharCode(v)));"
  "}"
  "const pipelineBuf = new Uint8Array([0x5E, 0x41, 0x02, 0x2B, 0x24]);"
  "const pipelineRegex = buildRegexFromBuffer(pipelineBuf, 1);"
  "assert.ok(pipelineRegex instanceof RegExp, ""pipeline returns RegExp"");"
  .

WRAPTHEREGEXINASELFCONTAINEDPROXY =
  "// ── 7. Wrap the regex in a self-contained Proxy ────────────────"
  "function wrapRegex(rx: RegExp) {"
  "  return makeSelfContainedProxy({"
  "    source: rx.source,"
  "    flags: rx.flags,"
  "    test: (s: string) => rx.test(s),"
  "    exec: (s: string) => rx.exec(s),"
  "  });"
  "}"
  "const wrapped = wrapRegex(/ab+c/);"
  "assert.strictEqual(wrapped.source, ""ab+c"", ""wrapped source"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(wrapped.test(""abbbc""), true, ""wrapped test"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(wrapped.test(""xyz""), false, ""wrapped test false"");"
  .

THEEDGENPARAMETERASTHEDOF =
  "// ── 8. The edge-n parameter as the 6 DOF ───────────────────────"
  "// n ranges over the 6 edge values"
  "for (const n of [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]) {"
  "  const t = edgeNTokenize(testBuf, n);"
  "  assert.ok(t.length > 0, `n=${n} produces tokens`);"
  "}"
  "assert.strictEqual(EDGE.length, 6, ""6 edge values = 6 DOF"");"
  .

SELFCONTAINEDNOEXTERNALDEPENDENCIES =
  "// ── 9. Self-contained: no external dependencies ────────────────"
  "// Everything in this file uses only Node built-ins."
  "// - assert: node:assert"
  "// - Proxy, Reflect, RegExp: standard built-ins"
  "// - TemplateStringsArray: standard type"
  "// No imports beyond assert."
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof Proxy, ""function"", ""Proxy is a built-in"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof Reflect, ""object"", ""Reflect is a built-in"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof RegExp, ""function"", ""RegExp is a built-in"");"
  .

THEWHOLETHINGASONEOBJECT =
  "// ── 10. The whole thing as one object ──────────────────────────"
  "type SelfContained = {"
  "  tokenize: (buf: Uint8Array, n: number) => Token[];"
  "  buildRegex: (buf: Uint8Array, n: number) => RegExp;"
  "  wrap: (rx: RegExp) => ReturnType<typeof wrapRegex>;"
  "};"
  "const selfContained: SelfContained = makeSelfContainedProxy({"
  "  tokenize: edgeNTokenize,"
  "  buildRegex: buildRegexFromBuffer,"
  "  wrap: wrapRegex,"
  "});"
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof selfContained.tokenize, ""function"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof selfContained.buildRegex, ""function"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(typeof selfContained.wrap, ""function"");"
  "const rx2 = selfContained.buildRegex(new Uint8Array([0x41, 0x42, 0x43]), 1);"
  "assert.ok(rx2 instanceof RegExp, ""self-contained buildRegex works"");"
  "console.log(""I-151: edge-n-tokenizer → TemplateLiteralArray → RegExp → Proxy/Reflect — passed"");"
  "console.log(`  edge range 0x2-0x7 = 6 values = 6 DOF`);"
  "console.log(`  tokenizer reads the buffer at edge boundaries`);"
  "console.log(`  tagged template produces RegExp`);"
  "console.log(`  Proxy handler forwards to Reflect`);"
  "console.log(`  self-contained: only node:assert imported`);"
  .
